+  # lane; on OUR lane (KNE + Arista ceoslab-operator) et-named kernel ports
+  # transmit but the punt path never delivers inbound frames to the control
+  # plane -- proven by boot test 2026-08-30: OSPF hellos visible in tcpdump on
+  # the peer's et3 AND counted by the interface, neighbor table empty, 100%
+  # ping loss. The fork's old eth override was load-bearing after all. This
+  # ONE declaration drives INTFTYPE, the wired link names and the interface
+  # map together, so flipping it back is the whole fix.
